<title>FRANCE: French consumer sentiment falls to minus 37 in Sep.</title>
<headline>French consumer sentiment falls to minus 37 in Sep.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>INSEE gave the following data on household opinions. A positive figure shows the percentage points by which the percentage of respondents saying things had improved or risen outnumbered the percentage saying things had worsened.</p>
<p>				     Sept  July June May   Apr Mar  Feb</p>
<p> Overall confidence index    -37   -35  -36  -38  -35  -33  -33</p>
<p> Past living standards	 -73   -73  -72  -71  -70  -64  -68</p>
<p> Future living standards     -45   -45  -44  -44  -40  -35  -35</p>
<p> Future unemployment	    79    77   60   67   67   66   56</p>
<p> Past inflation		  -54   -47  -42  -41  -38  -40  -39</p>
<p> Future inflation		-37   -44  -40  -36  -34  -35  -37</p>
<p> Good time to spend	    -35   -32  -32  -30  -28  -29  -32</p>
<p> Good time to save		52    50   56   49   47   45   42</p>
<p> Current personal finances    10    09   10   07   08   05   11</p>
<p> Past personal finances	-23   -23  -25  -25  -24  -24  -20</p>
<p> Future personal finance     -11   -10  -10  -13  -10  -09  -09</p>
<p> Ability to save		 -32   -30  -30  -31  -32  -33  -28</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5381</p>
